{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011Cg2iXiiwjFUZj5MXoD2Kn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. Let me analyze what needs to be done:\n\n1. **storage/storage.go** - needs to:\n   - Add context cancellation check in `Put` (reject canceled context without mutation)\n   - Add revision conflict handling (CAS - compare-and-swap): `expected` should match current revision\n   - Add snapshot independence (return a copy, not the actual map)\n   - Add concurrency safety (mutex)\n   - Validate key (no empty key) and revision (no negative)\n\n2. **api/api.go** - calls `s.Store.Put(k, v, rev)` without context - needs to pass context (but the external API `Update(k, v string, rev int)` should remain unchanged, so we need to pass a background context internally)\n3. **export/export.go** and **replica/replica.go** - both call `s.Snapshot()` without a context, so these also need context plumbed through.\n\nI'm checking the test files to pin down expected behavior: `storage_test.go` covers CAS semantics (first Put wins, stale/conflicting Puts rejected without mutation, empty key and negative revision rejected, snapshot independence) and concurrent access guarantees, while `cancel_test.go` likely covers context cancellation behavior.\n\nTestCancel confirms that a canceled context should cause Put to return an error without storing the key. Looking at `api_test.go`, I notice the external API (`api.Update`), `export.JSON`, and `replica.Copy` all stay context-free, meaning only the internal storage layer needs `context.Context` parameters while these wrapper functions keep their existing signatures.\n\nStarting the implementation in storage/storage.go, setting up imports...\n\nWriting store struct and constructor...\n\nWriting Put, Get, and Snapshot methods...\n\nUpdating API, export, and replica modules to thread context through Store calls...\n\nI'm also reviewing the concurrency test, which spins up goroutines hammering Put, Get, and Snapshot simultaneously, then verifies the final revision count matches expectations.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":119,"cache_read_input_tokens":15204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":119},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c709bcd9-5888-4350-9fd5-b4bae2834ec2","uuid":"d355a18e-79bc-4453-ba10-3dedd3f970bc"}
